    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23448" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭn-hortor</span></b> , ātus sum,
		1, v. dep., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to incite</i>, <i>instigate</i> to a
			thing: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alicui canes,</span>”
				<i>to set on</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 8, p. 209, 9</span></i>
			.— Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭn-hortātus</span></b> , a, um,
			with <i>pass. signif.</i>, <i>instigated</i>, <i>set on</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">canes in eorum exitium inhortati,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 9, p. 234, 15</span></i>
			.</div>
